                <pb facs="0829" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7133: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-01T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1926—7
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 1—1:52
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. My 103, March 1, 5 p.m. I have telegraphed consul general, Canton, approving
                    proposal in the concluding paragraph of his telegram on the assumption that
                    regret and assurances are to be expressed to him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
